# term: a terminal on COM2, with a modem at the far end (the runner's
# HayesPeer; the image built with COM2 the modem and the log on COM3): what
# is typed goes out, the echo and the answers come back through IRQ3 and
# SYS_WAIT. MAME's AT has no COM3 for the log.
program: shell
modem: hayes
keys: term\n{wait 10}AT\n{wait 50}ati\n{wait 50}atz\n{wait 50}{esc}
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs dosbox-x
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>term
Terminal on COM2 at 9600 baud; Esc ends.
AT
OK
ati
rx286 test modem
OK
atz
ERROR
A:\>
